Given two positive integer sequences A and B of equal length, find the minimum non-negative integer k such that B with k added to all elements is lexicographically greater than or equal to A.

Solution outline:
If B_0 > A_0, return 0.
Else, compute A_0 - B_0. Traverse both sequences until A_i and B_i are not the same. If B_i > A_i or there is no such i, return A_0 - B_0. Else, return A_0 - B_0 + 1.
O(n)

